1.12.1: level-12 HaldCLUTs convert; pjdeploy picks by version

First contact with the real RawTherapee collection: it ships level-12
HaldCLUTs (lattice 144), which the converter refused against the
engine's 128 cap. Raising the cap was wrong (a 144^3 cube is ~60MB of
text per stock); the converter now resamples large lattices onto 64
points trilinearly - endpoints exact, interior error second-order.
The first fix attempt (integer stride) was rejected by its own test:
143 intervals factor as 11x13, so striding cannot preserve the top
node, shrinking full scale by 1.4%. The resample audits at 0.44/255
worst node deviation (pure 8-bit quantization) against a synthesized
level-12 identity, and renders within JPEG noise of a native identity.

pjdeploy now selects the tarball by version sort rather than file
date, so a re-downloaded old tarball can never shadow a new release.
